# OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions. Leave values empty in this example.
# The connector appends /chat/completions and sends only model, messages, and stream=false.
# That is the shared subset used here. It does not mean every provider feature is interchangeable.
# load_model_settings() reads only the process environment (os.environ). It does not load a .env file.
# A private .env may store these three names, but the user or a future launcher must export them first.
# Do not commit credentials.
#
# Qwen OpenAI-compatible roots. Beijing and Singapore use the workspace
# domains recommended by the current compatibility docs. Replace {WorkspaceId}
# with the workspace ID, and use an API key from that same region.
# https://help.aliyun.com/en/model-studio/compatibility-of-openai-with-dashscope
#   Beijing:        https://{WorkspaceId}.cn-beijing.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
#   Singapore:      https://{WorkspaceId}.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
#   US (Virginia):  https://dashscope-us.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# DeepSeek, from https://api-docs.deepseek.com/zh-cn/ :
#   https://api.deepseek.com
# OpenAI, from https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/chat :
#   https://api.openai.com/v1
MODEL_BASE_URL=
MODEL_API_KEY=
MODEL_NAME=
